KG42.register("rules-24bf7a5d8423c1f33b3c1856",{"id":"13-consensus_product_differentiation::v141-c-R004","paper":"13-consensus_product_differentiation","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R004","mechanism_id":"M01","name":"Price-signal coordination","process_stage":"coordination","market_meaning":"The producer's current offered bilateral quantity enters the price-estimate update through the trading-reciprocity imbalance term. Scope: Producer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. Condition: During an RCI price update involving a producer's bilateral quantity. The consumer's current requested bilateral quantity enters the price-estimate update through the trading-reciprocity imbalance term. Scope: Consumer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. Condition: During an RCI price update involving a consumer's bilateral quantity. Performing the RCI updates requires sharing the producer's current offered bilateral quantity with its communication neighbor as part of the mandatory quantity-and-price message. Scope: Producer-side quantity submission for decentralized RCI negotiation. Condition: At each RCI iteration, for a producer and its communication neighbor. Performing the RCI updates requires sharing the consumer's current requested bilateral quantity with its communication neighbor as part of the mandatory quantity-and-price message. Scope: Consumer-side quantity submission for decentralized RCI negotiation. Condition: At each RCI iteration, for a consumer and its communication neighbor. Each agent must send its bilateral price estimate to its communication neighbor as part of the prescribed information exchange. Scope: Per-iteration communication between neighboring agents in RCI negotiation. Condition: At each RCI iteration. The participants' separately calculated price estimates for a given bilateral trade must agree, λ_nm = λ_mn. Scope: Individually calculated price estimates for the same bilateral trade in the fully decentralized RCI implementation. Condition: After convergence. Reaching optimality through RCI does not require sharing agents' internal production/consumption parameters or product-differentiation criterion parameters. Scope: Information disclosure in the RCI implementation of MBED. The iterative process stops when convergence is established; convergence criterion (26) is optional. Scope: Termination of iterative RCI coordination. Condition: When algorithmic convergence is established under the prescribed stopping criteria.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function coordination.price_signal under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.demand","bidding.supply","coordination.price_signal"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E001","source":"bidding.demand","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g02-e19"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E002","source":"bidding.supply","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g02-e19"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E003","source":"coordination.price_signal","target":"bidding.demand","type":"requires","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g02-e19"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E004","source":"coordination.price_signal","target":"bidding.supply","type":"requires","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g02-e19"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Consumer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. | Consumer-side quantity submission for decentralized RCI negotiation. | Individually calculated price estimates for the same bilateral trade in the fully decentralized RCI implementation. | Information disclosure in the RCI implementation of MBED. | Per-iteration communication between neighboring agents in RCI negotiation. | Producer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. | Producer-side quantity submission for decentralized RCI negotiation. | Termination of iterative RCI coordination.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g01-e31","v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e20","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e22"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"x-P-nm","symbol":"P_{nm}^{k}","meaning":"Bilateral traded quantity of agent n with its neighbouring agent m at iteration k; a positive value is a sale/production and a negative value a purchase/consumption, so for a producer agent it is the offered bilateral quantity (P_nm ≥ 0) and for a consumer agent the requested bilateral quantity (P_nm ≤ 0).","kind":"operational","domain":"Signed bilateral power; source sign restriction by role: P_nm ≥ 0 for n ∈ Ω_p (9d) and P_nm ≤ 0 for n ∈ Ω_c (9e). No numeric range is stated in the formulation.","unit":null,"indices":["n ∈ Ω (agent)","m ∈ ω_n (neighbouring agent on the market communication graph)","k (RCI iteration index)"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e17","v141-b-g01-e24"]},{"variable_id":"x-P-mn","symbol":"P_{mn}^{k}","meaning":"Bilateral traded quantity of agent m with its neighbouring agent n at iteration k, i.e. the counterparty-side quantity of the same reciprocity pair; it appears together with P_nm^k in the trading-reciprocity imbalance term of the λ-update, and reciprocity requires P_nm + P_mn = 0.","kind":"operational","domain":"Signed bilateral power (same domain convention as P_nm), with the sign fixed by the role of agent m; source reciprocity condition P_nm + P_mn = 0 (9c).","unit":null,"indices":["n ∈ Ω (agent)","m ∈ ω_n (neighbouring agent)","k (RCI iteration index)"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e17","v141-b-g01-e24"]},{"variable_id":"x-lambda-nm","symbol":"λ_{nm}^{k}","meaning":"Price estimate, called the trading price, that agent n holds for its bilateral trade with neighbour m at iteration k; it is the dual variable (shadow price) of the reciprocity constraint (9c) and is updated by the λ-update (11) and exchanged with the neighbour. It is endogenously computed by the algorithm, not a fixed input.","kind":"operational","domain":"Real-valued price estimate (dual variable of an equality constraint); the source states no sign or bound for λ_nm.","unit":null,"indices":["n ∈ Ω (agent)","m ∈ ω_n (neighbouring agent)","k (RCI iteration index)"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g02-e05"]},{"variable_id":"x-lambda-mn","symbol":"λ_{mn}^{k}","meaning":"Price estimate, called the trading price, that agent m separately computes for the same bilateral trade at iteration k; the fully decentralized implementation requires that after convergence the two estimates agree, λ_nm = λ_mn, which is enforced by the consensus term of the λ-update (11).","kind":"operational","domain":"Real-valued price estimate (as for λ_nm); the source states no sign or bound.","unit":null,"indices":["n ∈ Ω (agent)","m ∈ ω_n (neighbouring agent)","k (RCI iteration index)"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g01-e31","v141-b-g02-e05"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"theta-alpha-k","symbol":"α^{k}","meaning":"Sequence of positive factors scaling the innovation (trading-reciprocity imbalance) term of the λ price-estimate update (11); the source requires persistent excitation, i.e. the series of the sequence diverges. It is a tuning input of the decentralized RCI procedure, set ex ante by the algorithm designer and not negotiated.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"positive sequence with persistent excitation; no general closed form is given in the rule (case-study setting α^k = 0.01/k^0.01 in (27))"},"unit":null,"indices":["k (RCI iteration index)"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g02-e07"]},{"parameter_id":"theta-beta-k","symbol":"β^{k}","meaning":"Sequence of positive factors scaling the consensus term (λ_nm^k − λ_mn^k) of the λ price-estimate update (11); source requires persistent excitation, i.e. the series of the sequence diverges. It is a tuning input of the decentralized RCI procedure, set ex ante and not negotiated.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"positive sequence with persistent excitation; no general closed form is given in the rule (case-study setting β^k = 0.1/k^0.1 in (27))"},"unit":null,"indices":["k (RCI iteration index)"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g02-e07"]},{"parameter_id":"theta-epsilon-lambda","symbol":"ε_λ","meaning":"Positive convergence tolerance of the stopping test (24) applied to successive λ price estimates; the source defines it as a positive parameter without giving a value in the rule text.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21"]},{"parameter_id":"theta-epsilon-P","symbol":"ε_P","meaning":"Positive convergence tolerance of the stopping test (25) applied to successive bilateral quantity estimates P_nm; the source defines it as a positive parameter without giving a value in the rule text.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21"]},{"parameter_id":"theta-epsilon-mu","symbol":"ε_μ","meaning":"Positive convergence tolerance of the optional stopping test (26) applied to successive boundary multipliers μ_n of the coordination iterates; the source defines it as a positive parameter, gives no value in the rule text, and marks criterion (26) as optional.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e22"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The producer's current offered bilateral quantity enters the price-estimate update through the trading-reciprocity imbalance term. Scope: Producer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. Condition: During an RCI price update involving a producer's bilateral quantity.","expression":"λ_nm^{k+1} = λ_nm^k − β^k (λ_nm^k − λ_mn^k) − α^k (P_nm^k + P_mn^k) (11), for a producer n ∈ Ω_p with P_nm^k ≥ 0 (9d) and m ∈ ω_n; the term (P_nm^k + P_mn^k) is the trading-reciprocity imbalance (innovation) term that carries the producer's current offered bilateral quantity into the price-estimate update.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":["x-P-nm","x-P-mn","x-lambda-nm","x-lambda-mn"],"parameter_refs":["theta-alpha-k","theta-beta-k"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e07"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The consumer's current requested bilateral quantity enters the price-estimate update through the trading-reciprocity imbalance term. Scope: Consumer-side quantity feedback in decentralized MBED forward-market negotiation. Condition: During an RCI price update involving a consumer's bilateral quantity.","expression":"λ_nm^{k+1} = λ_nm^k − β^k (λ_nm^k − λ_mn^k) − α^k (P_nm^k + P_mn^k) (11), for a consumer n ∈ Ω_c with P_nm^k ≤ 0 (9e) and m ∈ ω_n; the term (P_nm^k + P_mn^k) is the trading-reciprocity imbalance (innovation) term that carries the consumer's current requested bilateral quantity into the price-estimate update.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":["x-P-nm","x-P-mn","x-lambda-nm","x-lambda-mn"],"parameter_refs":["theta-alpha-k","theta-beta-k"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e07"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C003","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"Performing the RCI updates requires sharing the producer's current offered bilateral quantity with its communication neighbor as part of the mandatory quantity-and-price message. Scope: Producer-side quantity submission for decentralized RCI negotiation. Condition: At each RCI iteration, for a producer and its communication neighbor.","expression":"F_nm^k = {P_nm^k, λ_nm^k} (23), sent by a producer n ∈ Ω_p to each neighbouring agent m ∈ ω_n at iteration k.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal","bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":["x-P-nm","x-lambda-nm"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g02-e19"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C004","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"Performing the RCI updates requires sharing the consumer's current requested bilateral quantity with its communication neighbor as part of the mandatory quantity-and-price message. Scope: Consumer-side quantity submission for decentralized RCI negotiation. Condition: At each RCI iteration, for a consumer and its communication neighbor.","expression":"F_nm^k = {P_nm^k, λ_nm^k} (23), sent by a consumer n ∈ Ω_c to each neighbouring agent m ∈ ω_n at iteration k.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal","bidding.demand"],"variable_refs":["x-P-nm","x-lambda-nm"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e07","v141-b-g02-e19"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C005","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Each agent must send its bilateral price estimate to its communication neighbor as part of the prescribed information exchange. Scope: Per-iteration communication between neighboring agents in RCI negotiation. Condition: At each RCI iteration.","expression":"F_nm^k = {P_nm^k, λ_nm^k} (23), for all n ∈ Ω and m ∈ ω_n at iteration k; the price-estimate component λ_nm^k is the transmitted bilateral price estimate.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":["x-lambda-nm","x-P-nm"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e05","v141-b-g02-e19"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C006","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The participants' separately calculated price estimates for a given bilateral trade must agree, λ_nm = λ_mn. Scope: Individually calculated price estimates for the same bilateral trade in the fully decentralized RCI implementation. Condition: After convergence.","expression":"λ_nm = λ_mn (after convergence)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":["x-lambda-nm","x-lambda-mn"],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e31"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C007","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Reaching optimality through RCI does not require sharing agents' internal production/consumption parameters or product-differentiation criterion parameters. Scope: Information disclosure in the RCI implementation of MBED.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e20"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C008","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The iterative process stops when convergence is established; convergence criterion (26) is optional. Scope: Termination of iterative RCI coordination. Condition: When algorithmic convergence is established under the prescribed stopping criteria.","expression":"Terminate when λ_nm^{k+1} − λ_nm^k \u003c ε_λ (24); P_nm^{k+1} − P_nm^k \u003c ε_P (25); μ_n^{k+1} − μ_n^k \u003c ε_μ (26); criterion (26) is optional.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":["x-lambda-nm","x-P-nm"],"parameter_refs":["theta-epsilon-lambda","theta-epsilon-P","theta-epsilon-mu"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e22"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C009","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"The factors α^k and β^k of the price-estimate update are sequences of positive factors with persistent excitation, so that the series of each sequence diverges. Scope: Tuning conditions on the λ price-estimate update of the decentralized RCI negotiation. Condition: For the λ-update (11) of the price-signal coordination.","expression":"α^k > 0, β^k > 0, and the series Σ_k α^k and Σ_k β^k diverge (persistent excitation)","formalization_origin":"equivalent_translation","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["theta-alpha-k","theta-beta-k"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e24","v141-b-g02-e07"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e07","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":2,"printed_page":"995","section":"II-A. Peer-to-Peer Trading","anchor_text":"m- The power set-points of an agent n are constrained by the ny power boundaries Pn and Pn, ms a Pn ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The role of each agent is restrained to either producer or consumer (P_n P̄_n ≥ 0) as it simplifies the following derivations. Hence, the decision variables are constrained in sign depending on whether the agent n is a producer (P_nm ≥ 0) or a consumer (P_nm ≤ 0)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e24","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p05-c2r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":5,"printed_page":"998","section":"III-B. Dual Updates","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON POWER SYSTEMS, VOL. 34, NO. 2, MARCH 2019 equality constraint (as in the dual a","equation_id":"(11)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"This is referred to as the λ-update, λ_nm^{k+1} = λ_nm^k − β^k (λ_nm^k − λ_mn^k) − α^k (P_nm^k + P_mn^k) (11) where α^k and β^k are sequences of positive factors such that any excitation is persistent, so that the series of each sequence diverges [12]. The tuning of these parameters is key to the performance of the algorithm and will usually be a trade-off between convergence speed and resilience to change of setup. The tuning relies as much on the value of the parameters as on the ratio between the two. The performance could be improved by using adaptive factors that adjust this ratio."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e31","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p05-c1r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":5,"printed_page":"998","section":"III-B. Dual Updates","anchor_text":"sists in updating the decision variables based on a gradient step im built on optimality conditions ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Compared to the dual decomposition of [18], the algorithm is here implemented in a fully decentralized setup. The consequence is that price estimates for a given trade are also calculated individually by each participant, even though after convergence, a consensus has to be reached on these estimates (i.e., λ_nm = λ_mn). This convergence of price estimates is ensured in the price update, (11), through a consensus term. The last term, the innovation term, ensures the enforcement of the equality constraint (as in the dual ascent method)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p04-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":"997","section":"III-A. Structure of the Method","anchor_text":"(10d) he m where λkn = (λknm)m∈ωn is the vector of price estimates of ly agent n at iteration k, p⊤n","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"where λkn = (λknm)m∈ωn  is the vector of price estimates of agent n at iteration k, p⊤n  is the transposed vector of pn and Dn = (pn ∈R|ωn |)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e19","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p06-c1r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":6,"printed_page":"999","section":"III-D. Operational Aspects of the Iterative Process","anchor_text":"privacy and support data security since very little information is shared and only with those agents","equation_id":"(23)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Here to perform the RCI updates, a minimum set of informa-tion is to be shared. As such, at each iteration of the process, the set F nmk  of information sent by an agent n ∈Ω to a neighboring agent m ∈ωn at iteration k must be the following:\n             F nmk = {P nm,k   λknm}                (23)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e20","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p06-c2r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":6,"printed_page":"999","section":"III-D. Operational Aspects of the Iterative Process","anchor_text":"TY MARKETS WITH PRODUCT DIFFERENTIATION 999 nt Interestingly, all the agent’s internal production/co","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Interestingly, all the agent’s internal production/consumption parameters (an, bn, Pn, Pn, . . .) as well as the criterion param-eters (cgn, γgnm) do not need to be shared in order to reach optimality. The RCI implementation of MBED creates a fully decentralized setup with limited exchange of information, which is a valuable aspect with regards to data privacy."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e21","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p06-c2r1__v141-a-M01-validation","page":6,"printed_page":"999","section":"III-D. Operational Aspects of the Iterative Process","anchor_text":"TY MARKETS WITH PRODUCT DIFFERENTIATION 999 nt Interestingly, all the agent’s internal production/co","equation_id":"(24)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The iterative process is stopped when the convergence of the algorithm is established. For that purpose, we deﬁne three positive parameters ϵλ, ϵP and ϵμ such that the algorithm will terminate when the following conditions are met\n        λk+1nm −λknm \u003c ϵλ                 (24)\n                 k+1      k\n         P nm −P nm \u003c ϵP                (25)\n                 μk+1n  −μkn \u003c ϵμ                (26)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e22","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p06-c2r2__v141-a-M01-validation","page":6,"printed_page":"999","section":"III-D. Operational Aspects of the Iterative Process","anchor_text":"terminate when the following conditions are met 9) λk+1nm −λknm \u003c ϵλ (24) s k+1 k P nm −P nm \u003c ϵP (2","equation_id":"(26)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"exception"},"source_text":"Criterion (26) is optional but can be used for a more precise monitoring of convergence. Similarly, it is common to use a dual convergence criterion only, with the understanding that primal and dual convergence are linked. Further work should be done to understand if it is also the case here."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p02-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":2,"printed_page":"995","section":"II-A. Peer-to-Peer Trading","anchor_text":"actual power network (being, e.g., transmission and distribution er grids, or possibly a microgrid),","equation_id":"(1)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"To model this trading scheme, the net power injection P_n of each agent n ∈ Ω is split into a sum of bilaterally traded quantities with a set of neighboring agents m ∈ ω_n, i.e., P_n = Σ_{m∈ω_n} P_nm (1). A positive value corresponds to a sale/production and a negative value to a purchase/consumption. The set {P_nm | n ∈ Ω, m ∈ ω_n} is the set of decision variables. To lighten notations P_n is also used for the whole set of transactions of agent n."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e17","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p04-c1r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":"997","section":"II-C. MBED Formulation","anchor_text":"SORIN et al.: CONSENSUS-BASED APPROACH TO PEER-TO-PEER ELECTRICITY MARK Pnm + Pmn = 0 ∀(n, m) ∈(Ω, ω","equation_id":"(9c), (9d), (9e)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"P_nm + P_mn = 0 ∀(n, m) ∈ (Ω, ω_n) (9c) P_nm ≥ 0 ∀(n, m) ∈ (Ω_p, ω_n) (9d) P_nm ≤ 0 ∀(n, m) ∈ (Ω_c, ω_n) (9e) where D = (p_n ∈ R^{|ω_n|})_{n∈Ω}. Ω_p and Ω_c are the sets of producers and consumers, respectively."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e18","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":"997","section":"II-C. MBED Formulation","anchor_text":"all trades can be made at different prices. Differences in price cen are mostly induced by product d","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The shadow prices of the reciprocity constraints (9c), denoted λ_nm, define the prices for the various trades. This implies that all trades can be made at different prices. Differences in price are mostly induced by product differentiation, but can also result from an incomplete trading graph through different price zones. Since the MBED is a convex optimization problem, it only admits a single optimum, which can be obtained by applying a wealth of centralized and distributed optimization methods."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e07","location":{"location_id":"src-8ce0608b1a-p05-c2r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":5,"printed_page":"998","section":"III-B. Dual Updates","anchor_text":"IEEE TRANSACTIONS ON POWER SYSTEMS, VOL. 34, NO. 2, MARCH 2019 equality constraint (as in the dual a","equation_id":"(11)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"where αk and βk are sequences of positive factors such that any excitation is persistent, so that the series of each sequence diverges [12]. The tuning of these parameters is key to the performance of the algorithm and will usually be a trade-off between convergence speed and resilience to change of setup. The tuning relies as much on the value of the parameters as on the ratio between the two. The performance could be improved by using adaptive factors that adjust this ratio."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-pricing","v141-a-M01-validation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"coordination.price_signal","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e24","quote":"This is referred to as the λ-update, λ_nm^{k+1} = λ_nm^k − β^k (λ_nm^k − λ_mn^k) − α^k (P_nm^k + P_mn^k) (11)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e07","quote":"Hence, the decision variables are constrained in sign depending on whether the agent n is a producer (P_nm ≥ 0) or a consumer (P_nm ≤ 0)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e19","quote":"at each iteration of the process, the set F nmk of information sent by an agent n ∈Ω to a neighboring agent m ∈ωn at iteration k must be the following: F nmk = {P nm,k λknm} (23)"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e24","quote":"This is referred to as the λ-update, λ_nm^{k+1} = λ_nm^k − β^k (λ_nm^k − λ_mn^k) − α^k (P_nm^k + P_mn^k) (11)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e07","quote":"Hence, the decision variables are constrained in sign depending on whether the agent n is a producer (P_nm ≥ 0) or a consumer (P_nm ≤ 0)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e19","quote":"at each iteration of the process, the set F nmk of information sent by an agent n ∈Ω to a neighboring agent m ∈ωn at iteration k must be the following: F nmk = {P nm,k λknm} (23)"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e19","quote":"Here to perform the RCI updates, a minimum set of informa-tion is to be shared. As such, at each iteration of the process, the set F nmk of information sent by an agent n ∈Ω to a neighboring agent m ∈ωn at iteration k must be the following: F nmk = {P nm,k λknm} (23)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e07","quote":"Hence, the decision variables are constrained in sign depending on whether the agent n is a producer (P_nm ≥ 0) or a consumer (P_nm ≤ 0)."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e19","quote":"Here to perform the RCI updates, a minimum set of informa-tion is to be shared. As such, at each iteration of the process, the set F nmk of information sent by an agent n ∈Ω to a neighboring agent m ∈ωn at iteration k must be the following: F nmk = {P nm,k λknm} (23)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e07","quote":"Hence, the decision variables are constrained in sign depending on whether the agent n is a producer (P_nm ≥ 0) or a consumer (P_nm ≤ 0)."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e19","quote":"at each iteration of the process, the set F nmk of information sent by an agent n ∈Ω to a neighboring agent m ∈ωn at iteration k must be the following: F nmk = {P nm,k λknm} (23)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e05","quote":"where λkn = (λknm)m∈ωn is the vector of price estimates of agent n at iteration k"}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e31","quote":"price estimates for a given trade are also calculated individually by each participant, even though after convergence, a consensus has to be reached on these estimates (i.e., λ_nm = λ_mn)."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e20","quote":"all the agent’s internal production/consumption parameters (an, bn, Pn, Pn, . . .) as well as the criterion param-eters (cgn, γgnm) do not need to be shared in order to reach optimality."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e21","quote":"The iterative process is stopped when the convergence of the algorithm is established."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e22","quote":"Criterion (26) is optional but can be used for a more precise monitoring of convergence."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"06cd4b41b46a4fd8ac3156500fb58b7cdbcedc84d48a18ff0ced10ae990a2909","applicability":"formalized","reason":"Rule v141-c-R004 (M01, process stage 'coordination') is formalized from the supplied B evidence, which is experimentally eligible but UNREVIEWED (source_status 'unverified'; no B source audit, no C2 review, no Agent E in this experiment), so every expression below is provisional on that evidence. The rule's source mathematics is transcribable without invention: (i) the λ-update (11), λ_nm^{k+1} = λ_nm^k − β^k(λ_nm^k − λ_mn^k) − α^k(P_nm^k + P_mn^k), whose trading-reciprocity imbalance (innovation) term carries the producer's current offered quantity (C001) and the consumer's current requested quantity (C002); (ii) the mandatory per-iteration message set (23), F_nm^k = {P_nm^k, λ_nm^k}, which fixes producer quantity submission (C003), consumer quantity submission (C004) and price-estimate submission (C005); (iii) the post-convergence price consensus λ_nm = λ_mn (C006); and (iv) the stopping tests (24)–(26), of which (26) is optional (C008). C007 (non-disclosure of internal and criterion parameters) remains not_formalized because the extracted internal-parameter list '(an, bn, Pn, Pn, . . .)' has lost the overline/underline boundary typography, so a non-disclosure expression in terms of the message set F cannot be written without inventing symbols. C.1's frozen graph is untouched: V, E, mechanism, market, stages, statements, roles, members and original evidence_ids are preserved; entries were only enriched with source expressions and references, and C001/C002 additionally carry the α^k/β^k persistence evidence already belonging to this rule. C.1's graph draft carried no typed variable/parameter objects (its field notes explicitly say this does not assert the source lacks them); x and theta are therefore added here from the source's own definitions: P_nm/P_mn are the source's 'set of decision variables', λ_nm/λ_mn are the individually estimated price duals of the reciprocity constraint (9c), α^k/β^k are the positive persistent-excitation tuning sequences of the λ-update, and ε_λ/ε_P/ε_μ are the positive stopping tolerances. One symbol (μ_n of the optional criterion (26)) has no node in this rule's frozen V and is deliberately not declared here; it is flagged for C.1/B. No graph relationship was replaced by invented mathematics.","bindings":[{"object_id":"x-P-nm","node_ids":["bidding.supply","bidding.demand"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E002","v141-c-R004-E001"],"rationale":"P_nm^k is the bilateral quantity agent n sends toward neighbour m: for a producer agent it is the offered quantity of node bidding.supply feeding the price signal through edge v141-c-R004-E002 (bidding.supply → coordination.price_signal, links), for a consumer agent it is the requested quantity of node bidding.demand feeding the price signal through edge v141-c-R004-E001 (bidding.demand → coordination.price_signal, links). The source calls {P_nm | n ∈ Ω, m ∈ ω_n} 'the set of decision variables', which fixes its operational role."},{"object_id":"x-P-mn","node_ids":["bidding.supply","bidding.demand"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E001","v141-c-R004-E002"],"rationale":"P_mn^k is the counterparty-side quantity of the same reciprocity pair; it belongs to the same two quantity nodes and enters the price estimate through the same two link edges, because the λ-update (11) uses the pair (P_nm^k + P_mn^k) that spans the producer side (edge v141-c-R004-E002) and the consumer side (edge v141-c-R004-E001)."},{"object_id":"x-lambda-nm","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E002","v141-c-R004-E001"],"rationale":"λ_nm^k is the content carried by the coordination.price_signal node for the bilateral trade (n,m); the two incoming link edges record that this price estimate is updated from (and fed back to) the producer and consumer bilateral quantities, exactly the coupling formalized in C001/C002."},{"object_id":"x-lambda-mn","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E001","v141-c-R004-E002"],"rationale":"λ_mn^k is the neighbour's own estimate of the same trading price; it is a second element of the coordination.price_signal node (individually computed by agent m) and enters the price update through the same quantity-driven link edges, driving the consensus term of (11)."},{"object_id":"theta-alpha-k","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"α^k parameterizes the innovation (imbalance) term of the λ price-estimate update, so it is an ex-ante tuning input to the price-signal node; no frozen edge records a data flow for tuning sequences, hence no edge is claimed."},{"object_id":"theta-beta-k","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"β^k parameterizes the consensus term (λ_nm^k − λ_mn^k) of the λ price-estimate update, an ex-ante tuning input to the price-signal node; no frozen edge records a data flow for tuning sequences, hence no edge is claimed."},{"object_id":"theta-epsilon-lambda","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"ε_λ is the tolerance of stopping test (24) on successive λ price estimates, i.e. on the state of the coordination.price_signal node; the frozen rule has no dedicated termination node or edge, so only the price-signal node is bound."},{"object_id":"theta-epsilon-P","node_ids":["bidding.supply","bidding.demand"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E001","v141-c-R004-E002"],"rationale":"ε_P is the tolerance of stopping test (25) on successive bilateral quantity estimates P_nm, which are the quantities living in the supply and demand nodes and fed into the price signal by edges v141-c-R004-E002 and v141-c-R004-E001."},{"object_id":"theta-epsilon-mu","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"ε_μ is the tolerance of the optional criterion (26) on successive boundary multipliers μ_n of the coordination iterates. μ_n has no node in this rule's frozen V (boundary duals belong to the clearing/boundary-constraint rules), so the parameter is bound only to the coordination.price_signal node that the stopping rule terminates, and the missing graph coverage is flagged in revision_requests."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-C001","node_ids":["bidding.supply","coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E002","v141-c-R004-E001"],"rationale":"The formalized λ-update (11) places the producer's current offered quantity P_nm^k (with the counterpart quantity P_mn^k) in the trading-reciprocity imbalance term. Edge v141-c-R004-E002 is the producer-quantity → price-signal link owned by this constraint; v141-c-R004-E001 is included because the counterpart quantity appearing in the same imbalance term is carried by the consumer-side link."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-C002","node_ids":["bidding.demand","coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E001","v141-c-R004-E002"],"rationale":"The same λ-update (11) carries the consumer's current requested quantity P_nm^k through the imbalance term. Edge v141-c-R004-E001 is the consumer-quantity → price-signal link owned by this constraint; v141-c-R004-E002 is included because the counterpart quantity in the same term is the producer-side quantity."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-C003","node_ids":["bidding.supply","coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E004"],"rationale":"Edge v141-c-R004-E004 (coordination.price_signal → bidding.supply, requires) records that performing the price-signal updates requires the producer's bilateral quantity; the formalized expression is the mandatory message set F_nm^k = {P_nm^k, λ_nm^k} (23) for a producer sender."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-C004","node_ids":["bidding.demand","coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E003"],"rationale":"Edge v141-c-R004-E003 (coordination.price_signal → bidding.demand, requires) records that performing the price-signal updates requires the consumer's bilateral quantity; the formalized expression is the mandatory message set F_nm^k = {P_nm^k, λ_nm^k} (23) for a consumer sender."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-C005","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E003","v141-c-R004-E004"],"rationale":"The price estimate λ_nm^k is the second mandatory component of the same message set (23); both 'requires' edges (v141-c-R004-E003 for the consumer-side and v141-c-R004-E004 for the producer-side quantity submission) carry the per-iteration communication mandate that this constraint formalizes."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-C006","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The post-convergence consensus λ_nm = λ_mn is a property of the price-signal node itself (each participant's individually computed estimate must agree). The frozen rule contains no edge between the two participants' price estimates, so no edge is claimed."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-C008","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The stopping tests (24)–(26) terminate the iterates of the coordination process, anchored at coordination.price_signal; the source provides no termination node or edge in the frozen graph. Criterion (26) is additionally defined on μ_n, whose graph representation is absent (see revision_requests)."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-C009","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"α^k and β^k parameterize the λ-update that lives on the coordination.price_signal node, so the persistent-excitation condition added by C009 is a condition on that node's update dynamics; the added constraint's only member is coordination.price_signal, and no frozen edge expresses a tuning-data flow."}],"revision_requests":["Stopping tests (24)-(26): the supplied text prints plain differences ('λk+1nm −λknm \u003c ϵλ (24)', 'P nmk+1 −P nmk \u003c ϵP (25)', 'μk+1n −μkn \u003c ϵμ (26)') whereas the C.1 content note reads them as absolute-difference tests ('|λnm^{k+1} − λnm^k| \u003c ελ'). B should re-extract the page-6 equation image to confirm whether absolute values/norms are present before (24)-(26) are used as formal inequalities; the expressions given here transcribe the extracted text without adding bars.","Criterion (26) is defined on μ_n, the dual variable of the agents' power-boundary constraints. This rule's frozen V has no boundary-dual node, so μ_n is not declared here and ε_μ is bound only to coordination.price_signal. C.1 should confirm whether μ_n belongs to this rule or to the boundary-constraint/clearing rules (e.g. v141-c-R002/R003), or whether a boundary-dual node must be added to this rule's graph.","Role-set scope ambiguity: Section II-C (9d)-(9e) uses Ω_p and Ω_c for producers and consumers, whereas Appendix B (30)-(31) uses Ω_p and Ω_c for prosumers and consumers. The producer/consumer scoping of C001-C004 follows the Section II-C meaning. Explicit confirmation from B/C.1 is requested before this scoping is treated as fixed.","C007 is left not_formalized: the statement enumerates the agent's internal parameters as '(an, bn, Pn, Pn, . . .)', whose overline/underline distinction (power boundaries P̄_n, P̲_n) is lost in the extracted text, so a non-disclosure expression in terms of the message set F would require inventing symbol typography. B re-extraction of that page-6 passage is required to formalize the non-disclosure property (the criterion parameters c_n^g and γ_nm^g are legible, the power-boundary symbols are not).","Case-study settings (27): α^k = 0.01/k^0.01, β^k = 0.1/k^0.1, η^k = 0.005, δ^k = 1 and the tolerances of (28) ελ = 0.001, εP = 0.01, εμ = 0.0001 are carried by validation evidence (v141-b-g02-e24, v141-b-g02-e25) and are case-study values, not market-rule parameters; they are therefore not entered as theta values here. C.1 should confirm whether such case values should be recorded on the parameter objects.","Units: the rule's formulation states no unit for P_nm (the case-study tables label P_n in kWh), so unit is left null for all x/theta rather than inferred. Confirmation of the intended power/energy units from the source is requested.","Classification of λ_nm/λ_mn: these are declared as operational variables because they are endogenous estimates updated by (11) and computed individually by each participant, not fixed inputs. If the review taxonomy prefers to treat price estimates as state parameters (theta) rather than variables, a reclassification is requested.","All evidence used here is experimentally eligible but UNREVIEWED B material (source_status 'unverified', no B source audit, no C2 review, no Agent E in this experiment). The expressions, sign restrictions, index sets and parameter roles above are provisional and must not be reported as having passed independent source review."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
